// sync.cee - commit every filesystem to its disk (roadmap M2: a disk root keeps only what has been committed). A whole
// user program in CeeSafe (roadmap 1.3 R2, the CeeSafe rule's offset for R2's C): the C it replaced, in behaviour.

@header("unistd.h")
extern "C" {
    fn sync();
}

/// Safety: `argv` holds `argc` strings (none are read).
@export("cosmo_program_main") // crt0 calls main: the link names this main (userland.mk, USER_CEE_PROGRAMS)
unsafe fn run(argc: i32, argv: *mut *mut CChar) -> i32 {
    sync();
    return 0;
}
